-- ============================================================================
-- JPetStore Production-Like Seed Data
-- ============================================================================
--
-- Purpose: Provides approximately 5MB of realistic, production-like seed data
-- for the JPetStore HSQLDB database to simulate real-world usage patterns.
--
-- This file simulates the following production endpoint behaviors:
--
--   POST /account/newAccount  (HTTP 201) -- New user registrations
--   POST /account/signon      (HTTP 200) -- Successful login attempts
--   GET  /catalog              (HTTP 200) -- Browsing categories/products
--   GET  /catalog/viewProduct  (HTTP 200) -- Product detail views
--   GET  /catalog/viewItem     (HTTP 200) -- Item detail views
--   POST /cart/addItemToCart    (HTTP 200) -- Adding items to cart
--   POST /orders/newOrder      (HTTP 200) -- Successful order placement (95%)
--   POST /orders/newOrder      (HTTP 500) -- Failed order placement (5%)
--   GET  /orders/viewOrder     (HTTP 200) -- Order history viewing
--
-- Transaction Status Distribution:
--   95% of orders: status 'P' (Processed/Passed) -- successful transactions
--    5% of orders: status 'F' (Failed)           -- failed transactions
--
-- User Distribution: ~750 users with long-tail order frequency
-- Order Distribution: ~10000 orders with seasonal patterns
-- Product Popularity: Cats and Dogs most popular, Reptiles least popular
--
-- Generated for load testing and production simulation purposes.
-- Compatible with HSQLDB syntax.
-- ============================================================================

-- ============================================================================
-- SECTION 1: USER REGISTRATIONS
-- Simulates: POST /account/newAccount (HTTP 201 Created)
-- Generates signon, account, and profile entries for ~750 users
-- ============================================================================

-- -------------------------------------------
-- 1a. SIGNON TABLE - User credentials
-- Simulates: POST /account/signon (HTTP 200 OK)
-- -------------------------------------------


-- -------------------------------------------
-- 1b. ACCOUNT TABLE - User profile information
-- Simulates: POST /account/newAccount (HTTP 201 Created)
-- Varied names, emails, addresses across US states/cities
-- -------------------------------------------


-- -------------------------------------------
-- 1c. PROFILE TABLE - User preferences
-- Varied language preferences and favorite categories
-- -------------------------------------------


-- ============================================================================
-- SECTION 2: ORDER DATA
-- Simulates: POST /orders/newOrder
--   HTTP 200 OK  for 95% of orders (successful placement)
--   HTTP 500 Error for 5% of orders (failed placement)
-- Orders span 12 months with seasonal patterns:
--   - Christmas/Holiday boost (Dec 15-31): 3x volume
--   - Black Friday/Thanksgiving (Nov 20-30): 2.5x volume
--   - Valentine's Day (Feb 10-14): 1.8x volume
--   - Mother's Day (May 5-15): 1.5x volume
--   - Father's Day (Jun 10-20): 1.3x volume
--   - Summer (Jul-Aug): 1.2x volume
-- ============================================================================

-- -------------------------------------------
-- 2a. ORDERS TABLE - Order header records
-- Simulates: POST /orders/newOrder (HTTP 200/500)
-- GET /orders/viewOrder (HTTP 200) for order retrieval
-- -------------------------------------------


-- ============================================================================
-- SECTION 3: LINE ITEMS
-- Simulates: POST /cart/addItemToCart (HTTP 200 OK)
-- Each order has 1-5 line items referencing existing catalog items
-- Item popularity weighted: Cats > Dogs > Fish > Birds > Reptiles
-- Simulates: GET /catalog/viewProduct (HTTP 200) and
--            GET /catalog/viewItem (HTTP 200) for browsing before purchase
-- ============================================================================


-- ============================================================================
-- SECTION 4: ORDER STATUS / TRANSACTION RESULTS
-- Simulates transaction outcomes for POST /orders/newOrder:
--   'P' (Processed) = HTTP 200 OK   -- 95% of orders (successful)
--   'F' (Failed)    = HTTP 500 Error --  5% of orders (payment/system failure)
--
-- Failure patterns:
--   ~60% of failures concentrated on ~20 'problem' users (payment issues)
--   ~40% of failures are random one-off failures (system errors)
-- ============================================================================


-- Transaction summary: 9500 successful (P), 500 failed (F)
-- Success rate: 95.0%

